Today offline covers every git failure that never produced a per-ref answer: an unreachable host, failed authentication (a bad SSH key, an expired token), and local failures such as a corrupt object or a full disk. Git first fatal line is in the message, so a human sees the cause, but the code alone does not distinguish them. Decide which cases deserve their own stable code (auth_failed? unreachable?), how to classify them from git output across versions and locales (LC_ALL=C is already set), and what the Last sync fact and tess doctor say for each. Classification lives in internal/git (Push and Fetch); the codes in internal/sync.